{#
  Tool-framing strip — collapsible "for exploration only" disclaimer.
  Documented in STYLE_GUIDE.md §6.11.

  Placement: between page hero and calculator inputs, after the page's
  main title and any introductory copy.

  Behavior:
    - First-time visitors: expanded by default with full disclaimer text
      and a × dismiss affordance
    - Returning visitors (sessionStorage flag set): collapsed to a small
      ⓘ indicator that can be re-expanded by clicking
    - sessionStorage scoped per-tab (intentionally not localStorage —
      the disclaimer should re-appear in a fresh browser session)

  Pages opt in by adding {% include 'components/tool-framing.njk' %}
  near the top of their content.
#}

<aside class="tool-framing" id="toolFraming" data-state="expanded" aria-label="Tool framing and disclaimer">
  <div class="tool-framing-collapsed">
    <button class="tool-framing-toggle" type="button" data-action="expand" aria-label="Show disclaimer">
      <span class="tool-framing-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#9432;</span>
      <span class="tool-framing-collapsed-text">For exploration only &middot; click to read full disclaimer</span>
    </button>
  </div>
  <div class="tool-framing-expanded">
    <div class="tool-framing-content">
      <div class="tool-framing-label">For exploration only</div>
      {#- COUNSEL EDIT 1, 2026-09-07 — extended, not replaced. The counsel pass
          on The Rundown found the site's one live exposure to be anti-fraud
          ACCURACY rather than any registration requirement, and closed it with
          boundary statements rather than with a change of voice. Three clauses
          were added here: the fee/spread/tax basis (the publisher's share of
          customary disclosure), the no-registration line, and the
          computes-in-your-browser line, which is the sentence that actually
          does the work — the publisher exclusion is satisfied by what these
          tools DO (client-side, impersonal, no execution) rather than by
          asserting it. "Commodity interests" is the CEA term of art and the
          list after it is not decorative: naming futures, options, swaps and
          margined positions is what keeps the CTA definition off the site.
          This strip is the site-wide disclaimer surface (28 pages); the full
          decision record is filed verbatim in OPEN_ITEMS.md. Do not trim this
          text without re-reading it. -#}
      <p class="tool-framing-body">This tool is for educational and informational purposes; nothing here is financial advice. Bitcoin involves significant risk, including potential total loss. Figures are before fees, spreads and taxes. Consult a qualified financial adviser before making decisions based on what you see here. Last Coin Standing is not a registered investment adviser, broker-dealer, or commodity trading advisor. Everything here computes in your browser: it does not custody, transfer, or execute transactions in bitcoin or any other asset, and it does not analyze or facilitate transactions in commodity interests — futures, options, swaps, or margined or leveraged positions.</p>
    </div>
    <button class="tool-framing-dismiss" type="button" data-action="dismiss" aria-label="Dismiss disclaimer">&times;</button>
  </div>
</aside>

<script>
(function() {
  var el = document.getElementById('toolFraming');
  if (!el) return;
  var KEY = 'lcs.toolFraming.dismissed';

  // Read dismissed state from sessionStorage (per-tab; resets on new session)
  var dismissed = false;
  try { dismissed = sessionStorage.getItem(KEY) === 'true'; } catch(e) {}
  if (dismissed) el.setAttribute('data-state', 'collapsed');

  el.addEventListener('click', function(e) {
    var btn = e.target.closest('[data-action]');
    if (!btn) return;
    var action = btn.getAttribute('data-action');
    if (action === 'dismiss') {
      el.setAttribute('data-state', 'collapsed');
      try { sessionStorage.setItem(KEY, 'true'); } catch(e) {}
    } else if (action === 'expand') {
      el.setAttribute('data-state', 'expanded');
      try { sessionStorage.setItem(KEY, 'false'); } catch(e) {}
    }
  });
})();
</script>
